{"text": "Translation\n\nSvenska Dagbladet, Stockholm\nMarch 30, 1978\n\nThe Warning Texts have made Effect\n\nMore and more Swedes stop smoking\n\nThe Swedish people smoke less and less. In one\nyear's time the share of smoking men has been\nreduced from 43 to 39%. The share of smoking\nwomen has gone down from 34 to 31%. Among young\npeople the women smoke more than the men.\n\nThis is the result of an investigation about smok-\ning habits made by the Social Board and the Na-\ntional Association against the harmful Effects of\nTobacco: (NTS).\n\nBesides. studying the total number of smokers one\nhas specially investigated how the warning texts\non the cigarette packs are influencing smokers\nand non-smokers. The statistical selection, which\nhas been made by Sifo, includes 2,000 interviews.\n\u2018Those who do not stop smoking completely have many\ntimes switched to milder brands. That is statistic-\nally ensured both for men and women.\n\nWarning Texts have Effect\n\nMr. Lars Ramstr\u00e9m, Managing Director of NTS, says\nto Svenska Dagblade\n\nWe have owing to our investigation found that the\nwarning texts have influenced the smokers and for-\ntunately also non-smokers, who can circulate the\ninformation.\n\nIt is, of course, a very gratifying tendency that\nsmoking is decreasing. This applies particularly\nto men, who have obviously decreased their smoking\nsince 1970 and now the women are following. How-\never, there are still more than three million smo-\nkers' in Sweden,\n\n2pSS26p202",
